<h1 class="article-title">Time Capsule Laid in Foundations of New Scania Latvia Service Centre in Liepāja</h1>
<div class="block_text mt-5 mb-4">
<div class="row">
<div class="col"><div class="col-12 output"><p>Scania Latvia marked the start of construction of its new truck service and sales centre in Liepāja by ceremonially laying a time capsule in the foundations. The project is important both for the company’s future development and for the region’s transport infrastructure and business environment.</p><p>The new Scania Latvia centre will be a major asset for the Liepāja region, becoming one of Kurzeme’s key transport service facilities. It will improve access to services for professional carriers, encourage regional economic activity and local business development, and support modern, safe and sustainable transport infrastructure.</p><p>The new facility will replace Scania’s existing Liepāja service centre, located only a few minutes away from the planned site at 1B Grīzupes Street. The approximately 1,300 m² building will have three repair and maintenance lines capable of servicing up to ten trucks simultaneously. It will also include a modern vehicle wash and comfortable premises for service and sales specialists. The total investment is EUR 4.6 million. The centre will provide high-quality service for diesel-powered, gas-powered and battery-electric trucks, along with their bodies and trailers.</p><p>The project responds to the growing regional need for high-quality, fast and technologically advanced transport maintenance services. As freight volumes and logistics activity in the Baltic region increase, demand for efficient service solutions continues to grow.</p><p>Scania Latvia Managing Director Aigars Pušinskis emphasised: “The new Scania service centre in Liepāja is a strategic milestone in our company’s development. It will significantly improve the availability of transport services in Kurzeme and, I believe, across the Baltic region. Our existing centre had reached its capacity, so building a new one was a logical step. Together with our team of specialists, the upgraded centre will enable us to deliver even higher service quality.”</p><p>Construction is being carried out by Mapri Būve. Board Member Holger Kald said: “There are three symbolic stages in construction: laying the time capsule, the topping-out ceremony, and opening the building. We plan for the new Scania Latvia centre to be ready by autumn next year. Winters in Liepāja are often mild enough to allow work to continue uninterrupted. Projects like this are extremely important for the regions: they create jobs, strengthen the business environment and stimulate investment beyond the capital.”</p><p>Raivo Špaks, Head of Business Development at Liepāja SEZ, added: “Manufacturing and port businesses in Liepāja SEZ rely on road freight transport. The regular Stena Line ferry connection between the Port of Liepāja and Travemünde, near Lübeck in Germany, is also important. It continues to develop, functioning as an extension of the German motorway network, with goods turnover valued at around EUR 4 billion annually. Construction of Scania Latvia’s new truck service and sales centre is clear evidence of economic activity in Liepāja and the region. Where there is demand, supply follows.”</p><p>Energy efficiency and environmentally friendly solutions are central to the project. Renewable-energy heat pumps are planned for heating, while solar panels on the roof will reduce electricity costs over time. Smart lighting systems will be installed inside and outside the building, adjusting to daylight levels and the movement of people.</p><p>These solutions will allow the new centre to operate more efficiently and reduce its environmental impact, while providing a modern workplace for employees and top-quality customer service.</p><p>About Scania Latvia:</p><p>Scania is a global leader in transport solutions. Working with partners and customers, the company is driving the transition to a sustainable transport system. Scania is part of TRATON GROUP. Further information: www.scania.com</p><p>Scania Latvia was founded on 2 March 1993. It sells new and used Scania trucks, provides warranty and post-warranty repairs and maintenance for Scania vehicles and combinations at service centres in Riga, Valmiera, Daugavpils and Liepāja, sells spare parts and accessories, offers vehicle financing and insurance in cooperation with Scania Finans, and provides driver training.</p><p>About Mapri Būve</p><p>SIA Mapri Būve is a fast-growing construction company operating since 2014 and specialising in residential, commercial and industrial buildings. As part of Estonia’s Mapri Ehitus group, it benefits from regional cooperation, shared expertise and opportunities to work on projects across the Baltic states. Mapri Būve employs 74 people in Latvia.</p></div>
